(P/'AUTHOR_METADATA_REQUIRED.md').write_text('''# Author metadata required\n\nThe manuscript remains anonymized as `Anonymous Authors`. Before submission, provide:\n\n- author names and order;\n- affiliations;\n- corresponding author and email;\n- ORCID identifiers if desired;\n- verified IRB/ethics statement or author-confirmed public-dataset wording;\n- funding statement;\n- competing-interest statement;\n- code/data availability confirmation.\n''')
(P/'cover_letter_draft.md').write_text('''Dear Editor,\n\nPlease consider our manuscript, “ShiftSleep-UQ: Calibration and Selective Reliability of Multimodal Sleep Staging Under Compound Dataset and Missing-Modality Shift,” as a regular paper for IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics.\n\nThe manuscript addresses a biomedical-health-informatics problem that is often hidden by in-domain, full-modality evaluation: how predictive and reliability behavior changes when sleep-staging systems face reciprocal dataset shift and missing channels. We provide a frozen two-dataset benchmark, target-free primary evaluation, subject-level uncertainty and selective-prediction analyses, conformal transfer diagnostics, and a controlled source-only modality-dropout comparison. The contribution is an evidence-bounded benchmark and reliability study, not a claim of a new architecture or universal uncertainty method.\n\nThe primary results show improved compound-shift macro-F1 in three of four prespecified cells, while calibration, error ranking, and conformal behavior remain heterogeneous. The manuscript preserves the inconclusive fourth cell, distinguishes deployable evidence from target-label oracle diagnostics, and provides a reproducible artifact and audit package. These properties align with J-BHI’s focus on biomedical and health informatics at the intersection of information technology and biomedicine.\n\nThis manuscript is original, is not under consideration elsewhere, and contains no invented clinical or prospective-validation claim. Author, funding, ethics, and competing-interest declarations will be completed before submission.\n\nSincerely,\nAnonymous Authors\n''')
(P/'submission_declarations.md').write_text('''# IEEE JBHI submission declarations\n\n## VERIFIED\n- The work is a benchmark/reliability study using public Sleep-EDF Expanded and ISRUC-derived evidence artifacts.\n- Raw source datasets are not redistributed by this repository.\n- The manuscript does not claim prospective clinical validation, clinical deployment, or unrestricted data sharing.\n- The canonical manuscript and venue derivative retain the frozen B0/B1 results and target-free primary protocol.\n\n## AUTHOR_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED\n- Authorship, affiliations, corresponding-author contact, and ORCID.\n- Exact public-dataset ethics/IRB wording required by IEEE JBHI.\n- Funding and grant information, or a confirmed no-funding statement.\n- Competing-interest disclosure.\n- Final code-availability wording and repository release scope.\n- Originality and exclusive-submission confirmation.\n''')
(P/'submission_checklist.md').write_text('''# IEEE JBHI submission checklist\n\n| Requirement | Official source | Status | File/location | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Regular paper category | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | PASS | main.tex | None |\n| IEEE two-column, single-spaced format | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | PASS | main.tex/main.pdf | None |\n| Abstract <=250 words | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | PASS | main.tex | None |\n| Numeric square-bracket references | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | PASS | references.bib/main.pdf | None |\n| Embedded figures and tables | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | PASS | main.tex/main.pdf | None |\n| 14-page limit including supplement | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/prepare-and-submit-your-manuscript/ | PASS | 10-page main + 2-page supplement | Confirm upload interpretation in portal |\n| Original/unpublished statement | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/for-authors/ | AUTHOR_INPUT_REQUIRED | cover_letter_draft.md | Confirm before submission |\n| Public database source/reference | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/prepare-and-submit-your-manuscript/ | PASS | main.tex/references.bib | None |\n| IRB/reference number statement if applicable | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/prepare-and-submit-your-manuscript/ | AUTHOR_INPUT_REQUIRED | submission_declarations.md | Confirm exact wording |\n| OA or Traditional choice | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/prepare-and-submit-your-manuscript/ | AUTHOR_INPUT_REQUIRED | submission_declarations.md | Choose later; no portal action taken |\n| Author metadata | IEEE Author Portal | AUTHOR_INPUT_REQUIRED | AUTHOR_METADATA_REQUIRED.md | Supply verified metadata |\n| Copyright form | https://www.embs.org/jbhi/prepare-and-submit-your-manuscript/ | NOT_APPLICABLE | post-acceptance | No action before acceptance |\n''')
(P/'highlights.md').write_text('''# Optional highlights\n\n- Reciprocal Sleep-EDF/ISRUC evaluation exposes compound dataset and missing-modality shift.\n- Source-only modality-dropout training improves compound-shift macro-F1 in three of four primary cells.\n- Calibration, selective reliability, and conformal transfer remain heterogeneous after predictive gains.\n- Frozen artifacts, subject-bootstrap inference, and target-free evaluation support reproducibility.\n''')
